From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:10:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/21] media: apple: vxd: split the command encoders out of the
 buffer pool

The H.264 command-stream builder (R3c) has to be checked word for word
against an independent reference generator on the host.  Move the
encoders, the chunk and packet-list helpers and struct apple_vxd_cmdbuf
into apple-vxd-cmd.{c,h}, which use no MMIO, no DMA API and no lock, so
the same file builds in the host harness.  apple-vxd-cmdbuf.c keeps the
pool, the packet -> mailbox message arithmetic, the self-test and the
debugfs view.

One addition for the per-picture chunks of single-register writes:
apple_vxd_cmdbuf_pair_chunk_end() closes a chunk made only of
0x000f0000 pairs with the 0x40 - (pairs & 7) * 8 byte pad of
0xfffffff0062b7ab0, and the writer now counts the pairs.  No functional
change otherwise.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>
